{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bouncy-peacockish-titmouse","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD`, per-criterion `block_threshold`/`default_posture` in `criteria_routing.json`, the execution-phase raise in `orchestrator.py`, `DEFAULT_ADVISORY_CAP`) is deterministic and every input it needs — the Pass-2 `verification` vector, `block_threshold`, `blocking_enabled`, `review_phase` — is in the v2 sidecar. `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` and `docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py` prove the replay works but are one-off scripts with hardcoded baselines. Any proposal touching Pass-3 logic or thresholds should be assessable over all ~4,300 reviews for free.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py`:\n\n- Input: the corpus + labels, and a **candidate** = a Python callable/module path for the decide function, a routing overlay JSON (thresholds/postures), and `[verify]` config overrides. Default candidate = current code, so \"replay current code\" is the identity check.\n- Run `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` (or `pass3_decide` per finding) for baseline and candidate over every review; keep the stored decision as the historical reference too.\n- Report (`tier0-<candidate-name>-<date>.md` + JSON): verdict flip matrix (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE), friction rate (share of reviews BLOCKed), per-criterion block/advisory/drop deltas, priority distribution shift, and label-proxy metrics — block rate on `escaped_defect`/`completion_failed_after_pass` tickets (recall proxy) vs block rate on `clean_close` tickets (false-positive proxy), and share of blocking findings that were `resolved_by_author`. Every delta is annotated against the noise band from the labels ticket.\n- Post-verdict floors (novelty/completion/drift) are replayed only when their inputs are present in the sidecar (`coverage.drift`, prior findings); otherwise reported as not replayed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py`, `report.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: identity replay of a fixture corpus yields zero diffs; a candidate overlay lowering one criterion's threshold flips exactly the fixture findings whose priority sits between old and new thresholds; a v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` is skipped and counted. E2E (manual, recorded in the report): replay the documented plan-v4→plan-v5 impact-model change and reproduce the effect recorded in `docs/calibration/`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero verdict flips against stored decisions for reviews whose `impact_model_version` matches current; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4→plan-v5 change reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report contains verdict flip matrix, friction rate, per-criterion deltas and the label-proxy recall/false-positive metrics, each annotated relative to the noise band; checked by inspection of one report.\n- [ ] A full-corpus run completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and by running without provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","id":"5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","priority":1,"tags":["plan-review","evals","tier-0","pass-3"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Tier-0 harness: replay Pass-3 calculation, thresholds and routing overlays over the whole corpus (zero LLM)"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788029128934029385,"uuid":"63cb9ce7-113b-4410-a805-1ed4155cb7d8"}